# Item table

The source of truth for items is the Google Sheet:
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1uPRXiHfty9kSLOXt1RiWTKBP9hps7g4SHuq4Qchq1eo/edit
Columns: id, name, tier, scope, description, stacking. Anyone with the link can edit it; update it
through the browser tool as described in `docs/items.md` ("Updating the sheet").

When the user says the sheet changed (or before item work), list the differences:

```bash
node tools/diff_items_sheet.js
```

Then apply each difference to `ITEMS` in `js/data.js` (`desc` = description, `stack` = stacking) and
implement any changed behavior in the game code, so the game does what the sheet says.

`items.csv` (project root) is generated from `js/data.js`; never edit it by hand. After any item change:

```bash
node tools/export_items_csv.js
```

If the game side changed something the sheet doesn't have yet (a code fix, a new item), update the
sheet and rerun `node tools/diff_items_sheet.js` until it reports a match.

Every non-equipment item needs a `stack` field: a self-contained sentence on how extra copies behave.

```js
{ id: 'dio', name: "Dio's Best Friend", ..., stack: 'Each stack is one more revive.', desc: '...' },
```
